========
OVERVIEW
========

The proposed architecture for FIBRE-BR islands in Brasil proposes using
NetFPGA servers both as virtualization agents and openflow swtiches. As
such, it is necessary to port the OFELIA Control Framework (OCF) to
multiple Linux environments. This branches aims to contribute with this
set of features: portability.

Initial work focus on installing OXA and running it on CentOS 5.x, as
necessary for the islands, but it can be extended to all components present
in OCF.

Ideally one should test for FUNCIONALITY during installation, but doing
so is not feasible considering ofver's simplistic architecture. As such,
different Linux distributions, package dependencies, and possible
variations on critical points are verified on ofver case-by-case.

Also, standards compliance is exploited in this branch. LSB tools are used
throughout ofver, and a LSB-compatible init.d script is provided for
maximizing portability (that's why most upstream software does not direcly
include init scripts).

For more information please see the changes in OXA's ofver scripts and
"osdetect" script.

